{"lines":[{"x":0.086419753097466273,"y":0.0347467606723314,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"w":0.061728394826253252,"t":"Test 3"},{"w":0.82098765055338541,"y":0.082744405232664908,"t":"Merchant ships were built to transport lots of cargo over long distances and at a reasonable cost.","x":0.084362141691701892,"h":0.016195524146054074,"c":1},{"h":0.017476100382451065,"t":"They had a wider hull, double planking and a solid interior for added stability. Unlike warships,","y":0.098837209489209599,"w":0.8189300028483073,"c":1,"x":0.084362168431813225},{"y":0.11773255798007121,"t":"their V-shaped hull was deep underwater, meaning that they could not sail too close to the coast.","c":1,"h":0.017441860778592999,"x":0.082304536675668671,"w":0.8230452473958334},{"c":1,"t":"They usually had two huge side rudders located off the stern and controlled by a small tiller bar","y":0.13332098600620501,"w":0.81496709187825522,"x":0.084291731201233427,"h":0.020008565680298185},{"w":0.81481480916341142,"y":0.1540047113184364,"t":"connected to a system of cables. They had from one to three masts with large square sails and a","c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.084362142649016508},{"w":0.83744857788085936,"c":1,"y":0.17137809200086429,"h":0.017667844522968101,"t":"small triangular sail at the bow. Just like warships, merchant ships used oarsmen, but coordinating","x":0.084362130722973633},{"h":0.017465828445129006,"t":"the hundreds of rowers in both types of ship was not an easy task. In order to assist them, music","x":0.082304528542012659,"c":1,"y":0.18895348821284874,"w":0.82098765055338541},{"x":0.084300524835661528,"t":"would be played on an instrument, and oars would then keep time with this.","y":0.20620898970643919,"w":0.65030893961588543,"h":0.018423450568820332,"c":1},{"w":0.82510289510091139,"c":1,"h":0.017667844522968323,"t":"The cargo on merchant ships included raw materials (e.g. iron bars, copper, marble and granite),","x":0.084362132564062234,"y":0.24116607773136756},{"t":"and agricultural products (e.g. grain from Egypt's Nile valley). During the Empire, Rome was a","y":0.25872093041944222,"h":0.017486372319773014,"c":1,"w":0.81687240600585953,"x":0.0843621549446011},{"y":0.27761627892381313,"h":0.015988372380376759,"x":0.084362135431296212,"t":"huge city by ancient standards of about one million inhabitants. Goods from all over the world","w":0.80658437093098945,"c":1},{"y":0.2935806831214931,"t":"would come to the city through the port of Pozzuoli situated west of the bay of Naples in Italy and","x":0.084362146949045785,"h":0.017465827883483387,"w":0.83950617472330724,"c":1},{"w":0.82315734863281254,"t":"through the gigantic port of Ostia situated at the mouth of the Tiber River. Large merchant ships","x":0.084304229765546856,"h":0.020550167321877977,"y":0.3112768434202936,"c":1},{"w":0.8211422729492186,"c":1,"h":0.021345093618152511,"t":"would approach the destination port and, just like today, be intercepted by a number of towboats","x":0.084290910383196457,"y":0.32897085418550254},{"c":1,"w":0.28868403116861979,"x":0.08404478957328361,"h":0.019269419783557451,"t":"that would drag them to the quay.","y":0.34753489659616399},{"h":0.016022611984234825,"x":0.084362150171974598,"y":0.38368669048278403,"c":1,"w":0.76543207804361979,"t":"The time of travel along the many sailing routes could vary widely. Navigation in ancient"},{"t":"Rome did not rely on sophisticated instruments such as compasses but on experience, local","h":0.019140164899882239,"w":0.77983535766601564,"c":1,"y":0.39958775005326452,"x":0.084362162339831639},{"h":0.019888595922535224,"y":0.41701530193400949,"x":0.084298219889797202,"w":0.83139984130859357,"c":1,"t":"knowledge and observation of natural phenomena. In conditions of good visibility, seamen in the"},{"w":0.83127573649088526,"y":0.43604651146680817,"x":0.084362131719577835,"t":"Mediterranean often had the mainland or islands in sight, which greatly facilitated navigation. They","c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888},{"c":1,"w":0.8251028951009115,"x":0.084362132593306383,"t":"sailed by noting their position relative to a succession of recognisable landmarks. When weather","y":0.4549418603193357,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"x":0.084249180862229031,"y":0.46986056499333317,"c":1,"t":"conditions were not good or where land was no longer visible, Roman mariners estimated directions","h":0.02251838037066245,"w":0.8376890563964845},{"w":0.80246912638346368,"x":0.084362144520731874,"t":"from the pole star or, with less accuracy, from the Sun at noon. They also estimated directions","c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.48969375738538679},{"w":0.7921810913085936,"y":0.50726744170088611,"t":"relative to the wind and swell. Overall, shipping in ancient Roman times resembled shipping","x":0.084362129158708304,"h":0.017467540902720735,"c":1},{"x":0.084362137507991028,"h":0.017441860778592999,"w":0.79423868815104171,"y":0.52470930216163569,"c":1,"t":"today with large vessels regularly crossing the seas and bringing supplies from their Empire."},{"w":0.03086419741312664,"h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"t":"62","x":0.084362139873683586,"y":0.90552325562743474},{"w":0.25052792867024742,"c":1,"y":0.95619871442209903,"h":0.02767260251533854,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.71930827958083488}],"w":2400,"h":3396}